@* Under the finished run's card: the included papers whose full text has phrases that read like instructions to the
   model (#366). The text is treated as data and no decision changed, but extraction and the citation check read it,
   so the reviewer is asked to look at what was taken from those papers. Below them, the papers whose full text had
   hidden text taken out before the model read it (#369). Nothing shows when no paper has either. Only strong flags,
   phrases aimed at the model, count; a paper that only names prompts is on file but not listed (#472). *@

@if (Flags?.Where(f => PromptSafety.AnyStrong(f.Flags)).ToList() is { Count: > 0 } flags)
{
    <details class="ui-card mt-4 p-4 text-sm sm:p-5">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-not-supported">
            @flags.Count included @(flags.Count == 1 ? "paper has" : "papers have") text that reads like instructions to the model
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">The text was treated as data and changed no decision. Papers about language models can quote such phrases honestly. Check what extraction and the citations took from these papers.</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5">
            @foreach (var entry in flags)
            {
                <li>
                    <span class="font-semibold text-heading">@entry.Title</span>
                    <span class="block text-xs text-muted">@string.Join("; ", entry.Flags.Where(f => PromptSafety.IsStrong(f.Pattern)))</span>
                </li>
            }
        </ul>
    </details>
}
@if (Flags?.Where(f => f.Removed != null).ToList() is { Count: > 0 } removed)
{
    <details class="ui-card mt-4 p-4 text-sm sm:p-5">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-heading">
            Hidden text was taken out of @removed.Count included @(removed.Count == 1 ? "paper" : "papers")
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-2 text-muted">A reader cannot see these characters, but a language model can. They were removed before anything read the text. Quotes are checked against the text without them.</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 space-y-1.5">
            @foreach (var entry in removed)
            {
                <li>
                    <span class="font-semibold text-heading">@entry.Title</span>
                    <span class="block text-xs text-muted">@entry.Removed removed</span>
                </li>
            }
        </ul>
    </details>
}

@code {
    [Parameter] public List<AuBtechReviewAgent.SourceTextFlags>? Flags { get; set; }
}
